Done! Here's what I implemented:

LiteDescriptionTool — a new tool wrapper in src/tool_wrappers.rs that augments tool descriptions with JSON format examples for small/local LLMs in lite mode.

What it does:
• When `effective_context_tokens() ≤ 16_000` (lite mode), each tool's description gets an appended example like `\n\nExample: {"command": "ls -la src/"}`
• Examples defined for 6 tools: bash, read_file, write_file, edit_file, list_files, search
• Unknown tool names pass through without wrapping — zero overhead for tools without examples
• The augmented description string is pre-computed at construction time (no per-call allocation)

Files changed:
• src/tool_wrappers.rs — Added LiteDescriptionTool struct, lite_example_for_tool(), with_lite_description(), and 5 tests
• src/tools.rs — Wired the wrapper into build_tools() as a final map pass in lite mode
• CLAUDE.md — Updated architecture section to list LiteDescriptionTool
